ssigned sports and graduate athletic training students in the athletic training education program; instruct these students in professional prevention, care and rehabilitation of assigned student-athletes as well as the certification and licensure process. Required to attend national NATA and Conference USA meetings and/or conventions to remain current in their field for changes that occur. Assistant Director - Event Operations Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Athletics and Coaching, Event Coordination Under the direction of the Associate Athletic Director for Capital Projects, assist in the planning, coordination, and execution of home athletic events across MTSU's 17 NCAA Division I sports and support daily operations of Athletics facilities. Serve as the primary on-site event manager for assigned sports and events; coordinate logistics with visiting teams, game officials, Athletics units, campus departments, contracted vendors, and public safety; support special events and external facility use; assist with operational planning for Athletics capital projects, including the renovation of Floyd Stadium; maintain Athletics inventory records; and assist with hiring, training, and supervising graduate assistants, student workers, and event staff. Night, weekend, and holiday work is required. Grants and Development Specialist Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Research and Sponsored Programs Provide direct support to CHHS leadership to identify, apply for, and manage pre- award tasks related to external grants and contracts and develop, manage, and implement fundraising and development activities for CHHS. Identify potential funding opportunities to include private donations, fundraising campaigns, special events, and federal, state, and private funders and present to CHHS Director. Work with Director to develop proposals based on identified funding areas, opportunities, or project visions identified and/or prioritized by the Director that reflect the CHHS mission and vision. Develop and execute task lists approved by the CHHS Director for a successful application with a proposal that is complete, competitive, and in compliance with university requirements.. Work collaboratively with Office of Research and Sponsored Programs which will submit grant proposals, following ORSP procedures and policies. Provide updates to Director on progress of sponsorship and development activities and grant proposals prepared and request information needed to complete all proposal components including the budget and all required supplemental materials. Develop electronic file management system for all fundraising, development, and grant activities. Perform other related duties as assigned. Desirable Related Experience: Prior experience in higher education administration preferred. Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
