      "description": "Counselor - Counseling Services - 10 Month - Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Counselor - Counseling Services - 10 Month - Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Kiosk mode Counselor - Counseling Services - 10 Month 498711 Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Counseling Services Administrative Add to favorites View favorites Job Title Counselor - Counseling Services - 10 Month Department Counseling Services Salary $49,770 - $61,962; commensurate with experience (10 month position) Job Summary/Basic Function NOTE: 10-month position, August through May / 37.5 hours per week: Provide short-term mental health counseling and crisis interventions to currently enrolled MTSU students. Provide appropriate referral services for students with mental health needs beyond MTSU Counseling Services' scope of care, followed by brief case management services to ensure continuity of care. Communicate with in-house professional staff/psychiatrists, insurance providers, and/or local care providers as necessary to effect referrals. Coordinate and facilitate counseling and skill-building groups for students. As requested, provide psycho-educational outreach presentations to classes, student groups, and faculty/administrative groups. Serve as a consultant to faculty, departments, and administration as appropriate, and perform other related tasks or special projects as assigned. Required Education Master's degree in psychology, counseling, social work, or marriage and family counseling. Required Related Experience Minimum nine (9) months experience providing direct mental health services to clients in a mental health related agency, hospital, university counseling center, or private practice setting required. Required License/Registration/Certification Has applied for licensure in the State of Tennessee as an LPC MHSP, LCSW, LMFT, LSPE HSP, or PhD/PsyD HSP, with the ability to be fully licensed in two years. If licensed in another state, the ability to become licensed in Tennessee within one year. Desirable Related Experience Three years of paid experience post licensure as an LPC MHSP, LCSW, LMFT, LSPE HSP, or PhD/PsyD HSP, providing direct mental health services to students in a university/college counseling center strongly preferred. Desirable License/Registration/Certification Currently licensed in Tennessee as an LPC MHSP, LCSW, LMFT, LSPE HSP, or PhD/PsyD HSP. Documents Needed to Apply Cover Letter & Resume Required MTSU offers a comprehensive benefits package, including but not limited to the following: Sick Leave Vacation Leave for Administrative/Classified Staff/12-month Faculty 13 paid University holidays Medical, dental, vision, and life insurance Retirement plans Optional 401K and 403B Deferred Compensation Plans Educational benefits for the employee and their spouse and dependents Click here for additional information. MTSU is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. Proof of U.S. citizenship or eligibility for U.S. employment is required before employment (Immigration Control Act of 1986). Clery Act crime statistics for MTSU are available at https://police.mtsu.edu/annual-security-report/ or by contacting MTSU Public Safety at (615) 898-2424. MTSU is a Tobacco & Drug-Free campus. This position requires a criminal background check. Therefore, you will be required to provide information about your criminal history to be considered. For individuals requiring reasonable accommodation to apply: In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation to apply for a position with MTSU, please call 615-898-2929 or email hrs@mtsu.edu. Application Review Date: October 21, 2026 Back to search results Apply Now First Name (required) 75e9ce6e Last Name (required) f5ea113a Email (required) 1d35274a Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? T