    "https://careers.mtsu.edu/jobs/psychology-clinical-tenure-track-faculty-murfreesboro-tennessee-tennessee-united-states-ad5af5c0-9e8d-446b-baf1-3731de5b4230": {
      "title": "Psychology (Clinical), Tenure-Track Faculty",
      "description": "Psychology (Clinical), Tenure-Track Faculty - Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Psychology (Clinical), Tenure-Track Faculty - Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Kiosk mode Psychology (Clinical), Tenure-Track Faculty 498681 Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Psychology and Human/Social/Protective Services Tenure-Track Add to favorites View favorites Job Title Psychology (Clinical), Tenure-Track Faculty Department Psychology University Expectation MTSU seeks candidates committed to innovative teaching, robust research/creative activity, and meaningful service. We also seek to attract culturally and academically diverse faculty who value working with diverse students. Salary The salary is commensurate with education and experience. Job Summary/Basic Function The Department of Psychology at Middle Tennessee State University invites applicants for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position (#120310) in clinical psychology at the rank of assistant or associate professor. The start date for the position is August 1, 2027. The successful candidate will join a department of dedicated faculty who support several popular undergraduate minors, two undergraduate majors, four master's-level graduate majors, and one graduate major at the specialist's level. Faculty in the clinical area also support the undergraduate mental health services minor, the undergraduate psychology major, and the clinical psychology master’s program. Located on the edge of the greater Nashville area, MTSU is an ideal setting for a wide range of research and service-related interests. Key Responsibilities Teach undergraduate and graduate courses, including both area-specific topics (e.g., psychopathology, cross-cultural clinical practice, evidence-based treatment) and broader departmental needs (e.g., general psychology, personality, biopsychology). Mentor students in thesis and capstone projects. Develop and maintain an active research program. Participate in departmental, university, and community service activities. Required Education A terminal degree in clinical psychology or other health services psychology field from an APA-accredited training program that also included an APA-accredited internship is required by the appointment date. Other Desirables Applicants with the following will receive special consideration. Eligible for licensure in Tennessee as a psychologist with the health services provider designation. Demonstrated interest in clinical training at the master's level. Demonstrated potential for external funding in research, community engagement, or contracts. Documents Needed to Apply To successfully apply, applicants must include a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and statement of research or creative activities (as appropriate to the discipline) as separate attachments when submitting the application. Special Instruction to Applicants If you need help with the application, please contact Mitzi Dunkley, Faculty Recruitment Specialist, at (615) 898-5128. If you have position-specific questions, please contact James Loveless at James.Loveless@mtsu.edu. MTSU offers a comprehensive benefits package, including but not limited to the following: Sick Leave Vacation Leave for Administrative/Classified Staff/12-month Faculty 13 paid University holidays Medical, dental, vision, and life insurance Retirement plans Optional 401K and 403B Deferred Compensation Plans Educational benefits for the employee, their spouse, and dependents Click here for additional information. MTSU is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. Proof of U.S. citizenship or eligibility for U.S. employment is required before employment (Immigration Control Act of 1986). Clery Act crime statistics for MTSU are available at https://police.mtsu.edu/annual-security-report/ or by contacting MTSU Public Safety at (615) 898-2424. MTSU is a Tobacco & Drug-Free campus. This position requires a criminal background check. Therefore, you will be required to provide information about your criminal history to be considered. For individuals requiring reasonable accommodation to apply: In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation to apply for a position with MTSU, please call 615-898-2929 or email emp@mtsu.edu. Application Review Date: 10/10/2026 Back to search results Apply Now First Name (required) 9813c15c Last Name (required) 386d5b29 Email (required) 6beb9fd1 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Administrative Assistant 3 - Tennessee Livestock Center Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Administrative/Clerical Support, Other Responsible for all department office work, including but not limited to, budget reconciliation and revisions; composition of all correspondence and memorandum, payment authorizations, purchase orders, and payroll paperwork; preparation of legal contracts and department statements; completion of department timesheets; answering telephone and greeting visitors. Associate Athletic Trainer Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Athletics and Coaching The Associate Athletic Trainer will report to the Associate Athletic Director of Sports Medicine. The position will supervise and coordinate athletic training services for student-athletes in intercollegiate athletic programs – primarily men’s basketball. Essential duties include but are not be limited to: assist with the prevention, treatment, rehabilitation, physician referral, and medical documentation of all injuries associated with assigned student athletes; communicate with coaches, student athletes, parents, staff and physicians within NATA and HIPAA guidelines; observe all athletic policy and procedures in accordance with NATA regulations as well as NCAA, Conference USA and MTSU rules and remain certified to perform these duties on a daily basis. Coordinate Concussion testing and baseline testing for all assigned student athletes; provide supervision of daily practice and game coverage, in season travel, and summer sports workout coverage for assigned student athletes as permitted by NCAA legislation. Required to be flexible and adapt to schedule changes as necessary. Serve as an approved preceptor within the CAATE accredited graduate athletic training program. Provide direct supervision of intern athletic trainers for assigned sports and graduate athletic training students in the athletic training education program; instruct these students in professional prevention, care and rehabilitation of assigned student-athletes as well as the certification and licensure process. Required to attend national NATA and Conference USA meetings and/or conventions to remain current in their field for changes that occur. Assistant Director - Event Operations Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Athletics and Coaching, Event Coordination Under the direction of the Associate Athletic Director for Capital Projects, assist in the planning, coordination, and execution of home athletic events across MTSU's 17 NCAA Division I sports and support daily operations of Athletics facilities. Serve as the primary on-site event manager for assigned sports and events; coordinate logistics with visiting teams, game officials, Athletics units, campus departments, contracted vendors, and public safety; support special events and external facility use; assist with operational planning for Athletics capital projects, including the renovation of Floyd Stadium; maintain Athletics inventory records; and assist with hiring, training, and supervising graduate assistants, student workers, and event staff. Night, weekend, and holiday work is required. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert c4b33962 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropd